                                "sense_id": "ccf3997b-b39d-3128-939a-ed5795a965b7",
                                "text": "The water pinpricked her face as she stepped into the shower."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e4b04fbf-3faa-361c-a2b3-b281754268f6",
                        "entry_id": "3d0eac7e-8b82-3fe0-adad-a73eb3d24e54",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To puncture with a tiny hole or holes."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1cc5e835-a798-45cc-a304-077efb44ce65",
                                "sense_id": "e4b04fbf-3faa-361c-a2b3-b281754268f6",
                                "text": "By now it was dark, velvety dark with a moon, a darkness pinpricked by the lights from the landing place now drawing rapidly closer."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7290ffcf-1fd6-4f1e-ba32-a542a428c3f3",
                                "sense_id": "e4b04fbf-3faa-361c-a2b3-b281754268f6",
                                "text": "He had always had to repress the urge to pinprick her enthusiasms."
                            }
                        ]
